{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You shall not pervert justice.</b> As its plain sense." "<b>You shall not show partiality.</b> Even at the time of pleadings — a warning to the judge not to be soft toward this one and harsh toward that one, one standing and one sitting; for when this one sees that the judge honors his fellow, he suppresses his pleas." "<b>And you shall not take a bribe.</b> Even to judge justly (Sifrei)." "<b>For a bribe blinds.</b> Once he accepts a bribe from him, it is impossible that his heart not incline toward him to reverse in his favor." "<b>The words of the righteous.</b> Words that are made straight — judgments of truth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:23.168767916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}